-(`MISSING` and `MALFORMED` sit outside this derivation — they are registration and contract faults.) Automatic selection runs READY sets in scheduler order and passes over DONE, DEFERRED, and AWAITING-APPROVAL sets; only when no READY set exists may a no-argument implement select a single unambiguous Human-blocked Task set for attended help, and only when the block is an open HITL task rather than an unresolved AFK dependency. Multiple Human-blocked Task sets are ambiguous and require an explicit target. Draining stops when its selected set reaches DONE, FAILED, BLOCKED, AWAITING-APPROVAL, VERIFY-FAILED, or DEFERRED, or when an **Agent quota pause** interrupts draining without changing task status. At a BLOCKED HITL gate, interactive runs show a **HITL gate prompt** while non-interactive runs and `--yes` preserve stop-and-advice output and never auto-start attended assistance.
+(`MISSING` and `MALFORMED` sit outside this derivation — they are registration and contract faults.) A READY set that declared `"explore": true` reads **EXPLORE-FAILED** instead when its **Explore phase** gave up without writing the **Exploration report** — derived from its latest **Captured run** of phase `explore` and the absent report, never stored. It is not BLOCKED: no human owes a decision; the set needs a map. Automatic selection runs READY sets in scheduler order and passes over DONE, DEFERRED, AWAITING-APPROVAL, and EXPLORE-FAILED sets; only when no READY set exists may a no-argument implement select a single unambiguous Human-blocked Task set for attended help, and only when the block is an open HITL task rather than an unresolved AFK dependency. Multiple Human-blocked Task sets are ambiguous and require an explicit target. Draining stops when its selected set reaches DONE, FAILED, BLOCKED, AWAITING-APPROVAL, VERIFY-FAILED, EXPLORE-FAILED, or DEFERRED, or when an **Agent quota pause** interrupts draining without changing task status. At a BLOCKED HITL gate, interactive runs show a **HITL gate prompt** while non-interactive runs and `--yes` preserve stop-and-advice output and never auto-start attended assistance.
 
 **Tasks readiness**:
 The **Doctor status** of the `pop tasks` command family. Because the tasks feature is aimed at Git projects and its central workflow is agent execution from a **Runtime path**, Doctor reports `pop tasks` as Blocked when no Git runtime checkout can be resolved, even if read-only status rendering could still inspect local artifacts.
@@ -778,6 +778,22 @@ _Avoid_: Review episode, refine cycle, refine generation
 Formerly the Review pointer: the **Refine report** as every surface other than a reader carries it — its path and the instant it was written, never a line of what it says. Staleness is tolerated for the same reason as before — a report of a tree that has since moved is still worth reading — and the report itself now names the SHA it describes.
 _Avoid_: Review pointer, review link, latest review
 
+**Explore phase**:
+The pass that maps the code a **Task set**'s tasks will touch before anyone builds them (ADR-0262): a fresh **Explorer** is handed the set's manifest listing, every task body and the spec, and its answer becomes the set's **Exploration report**. It files its **Captured runs** under phase `explore` and spends against a retry cap of its own, beside implement, verify and refine. A **Drain** runs it at its head, before the first task is selected, when the set declares `"explore": true` and has no report yet; a report already there is reused as it is, and nothing compares the tree it records to the checkout. Gated by `[work.explore].enabled`, which defaults on, and skipped for a **Human completion**. `pop tasks explore <set>` runs it by hand on any set, whatever the set's `explore` key says, and replaces the report already there; a pass that is interrupted or fails writes nothing. It is the one agent phase that can stop a Drain: a pass that spends its retry cap without a report parks the set at EXPLORE-FAILED and appends one set-level **Progress record** naming the phase and the reason. A pass interrupted, or one no agent could start, does not park. Three doors leave the park: a hand-run pass that writes the report, `pop tasks implement <set> --skip-explore` (drains once, unexplored), and `"explore": false`.
+_Avoid_: discovery, research pass, planning pass
+
+**Explorer**:
+The agent that performs the **Explore phase**, in a fresh context and under the read-only agent posture: it reads the checkout and changes nothing, and pop writes what it answers. It is asked for the code as found — where things live, which seam owns what, the invariants that hold, the test shape, which files to read in ranges — in about a page, every claim naming a path or a symbol. It is asked for nothing about prior art (ADR-0262 decision 7).
+_Avoid_: scout, mapper, researcher
+
+**Exploration report**:
+`exploration.md`, flat in the set directory beside the spec and the **Progress record**: one **Explorer**'s map of the code before the set was built, headed by the facts pop stamps (set, when, **Work SHA**, Explorer) and opening with the tree it describes in prose. Each pass replaces it; there is no history directory. A builder edits it only to correct a line its own work falsified.
+_Avoid_: exploration notes, code map, context doc
+
+**Explore mark**:
+Whether a **Task set** that declared `"explore": true` has its **Exploration report**, carried beside its status as the **Verification mark** and the **Refine mark** are: `explored`, or `unexplored` with its reason as detail beside it — not yet run, or the pass failed. A set that never declared carries no mark. `ResolveExploreMark` derives it once per refresh from the report on disk and the latest **Captured run** of phase `explore`; the dashboard row, its detail view, `pop work status`, `pop tasks status` and the sign-off gate all read that one answer, and the EXPLORE-FAILED park is its failed reason on a READY set. Where it names the report it gives a pointer — path and the tree the report records — never the body.
+_Avoid_: exploration status, explored flag
+
 **Refine commit**:
 The runner-made commit capturing one **Refine** pass's in-place fixes: one commit per pass, subject rendered under the resolved commits convention, the set named in a trailer — agents never commit, so the **Refiner**'s edits reach history the same way an Implementer's do, and the tree is clean when the verify phase reads it. A prior verify PASS is not invalidated by it: within a **verification episode** the PASS stands and the **Verified-at SHA** badge shows the drift, exactly as for any other commit past a PASS. In the automatic flow this is moot — Refine precedes verify, so a pass's edits are verified together with the work they refine.
 _Avoid_: polish commit, style commit, fix commit
